VENDORED: plotly.js v2.35.2, cartesian distribution (web/vendor/plotly.min.js)

Used only by the browser front end (issue F_0003) to draw figures; it is not part
of the published library artifacts, and no Scala code binds to it -- the facade
emits Plotly's plain-JSON input, so nothing here is derived from its source.

Vendored rather than loaded from a CDN so the page has no third-party origin,
works offline, and cannot break when someone else's CDN changes. This is the
`cartesian` distribution, which carries the 2-D trace types Leonardo uses; the
full distribution would add 3-D at roughly three times the weight.

